1
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:57,428
After all these years, all your questions will finally be answered.

2
00:07:42,857 --> 00:07:48,857
Hey Arnold! The Jungle Movie is a family, comedy,
animation film directed by Raymie Muzquiz.

3
00:11:34,285 --> 00:11:40,285
When their trip to San Lorenzo takes a turn for the worst, Arnold and his classmate’s only hope of
getting home is retracing the dangerous path that led to Arnold's parents' disappearance.

4
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Arnold (voice), played by Mason Cotton.

5
00:19:17,142 --> 00:19:23,142
Gerald (voice), played by Benjamin Flores Jr..

6
00:23:08,571 --> 00:23:14,571
Helga (voice), played by Francesca Marie Smith.

7
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:06,000
Phoebe (voice), played by Anndi McAfee.

8
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
Eduardo (voice), played by Carlos Alazraqui.

9
00:34:42,857 --> 00:34:48,857
La Sombra (voice), played by Alfred Molina.

10
00:38:34,285 --> 00:38:40,285
Hey Arnold!: The Movie is a 2002 American animated adventure comedy film based
on the animated television series created by Craig Bartlett.

11
00:42:25,714 --> 00:42:31,714
It was directed by Tuck Tucker and written by Bartlett and Steve
Viksten, with music by series composer Jim Lang.

12
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
The film stars Spencer Klein, Francesca Smith, Jamil Walker Smith, Dan
Castellaneta, Tress MacNeille, Paul Sorvino, and Jennifer Jason Leigh.

13
00:50:08,571 --> 00:50:14,571
The film follows Arnold, Gerald, and Helga on a quest to save their neighborhood from a
greedy developer who plans on converting it into a huge shopping mall.

14
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
The events of the film take place during the series' fifth and final season.

15
00:57:51,428 --> 00:57:57,428
The project was originally developed as a television film titled Arnold Saves the Neighborhood, but
following successful test screenings, Paramount Pictures decided on a theatrical release.

16
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Hey Arnold!: The Movie was released in theaters on June 28, 2002,
and received unfavorable reviews from critics.

17
01:05:34,285 --> 01:05:40,285
The film grossed $15 million against a production budget of $3–$4 million.

18
01:09:25,714 --> 01:09:31,714
A made for television sequel, Hey Arnold!: The Jungle Movie, aired in 2017.

19
01:13:17,142 --> 01:13:23,142
The film explores themes of sequel, based on cartoon,
series finale, based on tv series.

20
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
The tone is lighthearted.
